menuconfig ION
	bool "Ion Memory Manager"
	depends on HAS_DMA && MMU
	select GENERIC_ALLOCATOR
	select DMA_SHARED_BUFFER
	help
	  Choose this option to enable the ION Memory Manager,
	  used by Android to efficiently allocate buffers
	  from userspace that can be shared between drivers.
	  If you're not using Android its probably safe to
	  say N here.

config ION_LEGACY_SUPPORT
	bool "ION legacy userspace heap mask compatibility support"
	depends on ION
	default y if ARCH_SM8150 || ARCH_SDM845
	help
	  Enable compatibility translation for Android 9/10 (kernel 4.9/4.19)
	  userspace vendor blobs that allocate ION memory using legacy heap masks
	  (such as legacy CAMERA, AUDIO, ADSP, QSEECOM, and CP_MM heaps).
	  This remaps legacy heap masks to the 5.4 compact heap layout.
	  Defaults to Y for SM8150 and SDM845.
	  If unsure, say Y if using vendor blobs built for 4.19/4.9 kernels.

source "drivers/staging/android/ion/heaps/Kconfig"

